    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated on the Rock Road, linking the main KilrushKillimer road with the coast road, this detached two-storey home is set on approximately 6.06 hectares (14.97 acres) under Folio CE7507, just 1.6 km from Kilrush town.\n\nExtending to approximately 137.63 sq. m., the dwelling retains many original features including high ceilings, timber flooring and window surrounds, decorative coving and traditional cast iron fireplaces. Accommodation comprises of an entrance hallway, two reception rooms, kitchen/dining room, pantry, utility, WC and bathroom at ground floor level, with three bedrooms, main bathroom and storage area on the first floor.\n\nThe property is approached through wrought iron gates onto a pea gravel driveway, with mature trees, hedging and lawns and an enclosed rear garden separated from the farmyard. The lands wrap around the residence and are divided into four paddock areas with secure boundaries and two gated entrances from the road. Farm buildings include a hay barn with lean to, cattle shed, a storage shed and cattle crush. A smaller paddock beside the residence offers potential for a residential site, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nKilrush town centre is approximately 1.8 km away, offering a wide range of shops, schools, cafés and recreational amenities, while Vandeleur Walled Garden is approximately 1 km and Cappa Pier approximately 1.5 km from the property. This is an attractive residential and agricultural holding combining a character home, almost 16 acres, useful outbuildings and excellent proximity to Kilrush with viewing highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL002295"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nFront Hallway - 6.1m x 1.95m\nProperty accessed via timber style door with glass panels either side, ceiling height of 2.85mt, tile flooring, decorative ceiling coving with centre rose feature, dado rail, timber stairs leading to first floor landing, door to reception room one, two and kitchen dining.\n\nReception Room One - 5.25m x 3.6m\n2.85 mt ceiling height, carpeted flooring, dual aspect windows to the front and side with timber surround, traditional fireplace with cast iron surround, tile insert and overhead wall mounted ornate mirror, decorative ceiling coving and high dado rail.\n\nReception Room Two - 4.1m x 3.9m\nTimber style flooring, front and side aspect windows with timber panelling surround, high ceiling, decorative ceiling coving, original cast iron fireplace with overhead wall mounted mirror with electric fire insert.\n\nRear Hallway - \nGives access to under stairs storage and access to the kitchen.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 4.75m x 4.50m\nTile flooring, two side aspect windows, built-in wall and base units, tile splash back, single drainer sink with mixer tap, space for fridge, door to pantry and door to utility.\n\nPantry - 3.60m x 1.45m\nTimber flooring and side aspect window.\n\nUtility Room - 4.1m x 4.55m\nTile flooring, half wall tiling, rear aspect window, side door access, sink with base storage, tile splash, space and plumbing for washing machine, ceiling to floor storage, door to wc and door to bathroom.WC - Tile flooring, rear aspect window, half wall tiling and low level wc. Bathroom - Tile flooring, rear aspect window, half wall tiling, wash hand basin with overhead mirror, corner fitted bath with timber panelling and separate shower unit with electric shower.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 4.8m x 1.95m\nTraditional timber flooring, doors to bedrooms one, two and three, main bathroom and storage area.\n\nBedroom One - 4.45m x 3.90m\nTraditional timber flooring, window to the rear and storage into the eves.\n\nStorage Area - 3.40m x 2.85m\nTimber flooring, built-in shelving units and houses water tank.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.75m x 2.8m\nPolished timber flooring and side aspect window.\n\nMain Bathroom - 8.7m x 2.25m\nPolished timber flooring, side aspect window, low level wc, wash hand basin, corner bath unit and wall mounted shelf.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.9m x 3.8m\nPolished timber flooring and side aspect window.\n\nOutside - \nFront - Block wall boundary with wrought iron railings and wrought iron gates, pea gravel driveway, mature trees, hedging and lawns.Farmyard - Hayshed with lean too, cattle shed, cattle crush, storage shed and ample gates and land divided into four paddocks. They elevate up from the road and has approximately 500m of frontage along the road heading down to the Cappagh Road. Fields are well laid out with good natural boundaries.\n\n"
      },
